# Code owners — ailuracollective/standards
#
# Every file here is load-bearing for every repository in the organisation. A
# change to a heading in a pull request template changes what every contributor
# in every repository is required to write; a change to labels.yml changes what
# every repository can label. There is no file in this repository that is safe
# to change casually.
#
# The rules below all resolve to the same single owner today, because
# @SiddharthaGF is currently the only collaborator with write access. The
# grouping is therefore documentation rather than enforcement: it records which
# files carry which blast radius, so adding a second owner later is a one-line
# change per group rather than a redesign.
#
# Syntax follows gitignore rules and the LAST matching pattern wins, so the
# catch-all comes first and the specific rules follow it.

/**                      @SiddharthaGF

# CODEOWNERS owns itself. Without this rule, a pull request that removes a
# reviewer's own required approval could be merged by that reviewer, because
# the rule that would have demanded their review is the thing being deleted.
/.github/CODEOWNERS      @SiddharthaGF

# Pull request templates — the widest blast radius in the repository. The
# body-structure gate in ailuracollective/actions/pull-request@v1 resolves
# these files from the consuming repository and requires every heading declared
# here to appear in a pull request body. Renaming or removing a heading changes
# the contract for every open and future pull request across the organisation.
/.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE/*.md   @SiddharthaGF

# labels.yml — the label set. Mirrored by hand into every consuming repository's
# manifest AND into the type-labels input of its policy.yml. A change here that
# is not mirrored makes a gate unsatisfiable rather than merely strict.
/.github/labels.yml     @SiddharthaGF

# Issue templates — the forms in the issue chooser. Renaming a body field id
# breaks bookmarked and prefilled links, and GitHub drops a label named here
# without an error when the repository does not have it, so label changes in
# these files are invisible until someone files a test issue.
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/*.yml        @SiddharthaGF

# ISSUE_STANDARD.md — prose, not data. It does not parse as YAML by design and
# is not read by any tool, which means nothing validates the type list against
# the templates. Editing it deserves the same care as editing a template.
/.github/ISSUE_STANDARD.md           @SiddharthaGF

# AGENTS.md — the instructions every agent and contributor reads before touching
# this repository. A wrong claim in here propagates into every repository that
# copies these files.
/AGENTS.md               @SiddharthaGF